It seems to be a tileset designed for nethack and not for slash'em.
Apparently, nethack and slash'em do not work exactly the same way  
concerning tile set. Among other things, the absurdXX.bmp files provided  
for the absurd tileset are regular .bmp images while the x11(big)tiles  
files for slash'em aren't :

jym@xrousse:/usr/local/slashemdir$ file x11*
x11bigtiles: data
x11tiles:    GLS_BINARY_MSB_FIRST

jym@xrousse:/usr/local/slashemdir$ file ~/download/absurd/absurd64.bmp
/home/jym/download/absurd/absurd64.bmp: PC bitmap data, Windows 3.x  
format, 2560 x 1920 x 32

jym@xrousse:~/download$ file absurd64.xpm
absurd64.xpm: X pixmap image text

(and, some tiles are specific for slash'em and thus aren't in the absurd  
tileset...)

